# MCP and security boundary

## MCP usage

- Use only MCP servers listed in `.cursor/mcp.json` (or Windsurf equivalent) and approved in `platform/architecture/mcp-policy.md`.
- **Least privilege:** read-only where possible; write only to paths allowed by policy.
- Do not add new MCP servers without security review (see platform deployment docs).

## Data classes

| Class | Rule |
|-------|------|
| `restricted` | No upload to external models; on-prem processing only |
| `internal` | No public URLs in fetch; audit log expected |
| `public` | External fetch allowed only if MCP approved |

## Prohibited without explicit user approval

- Sending PII, credentials, or full meeting recordings to external APIs.
- `git push`, deploy, or merge to protected branches.
- Reading paths in `boundary.forbidden_paths`.

## When AI must defer to human

- Final sign-off to customer.
- Production deployment.
- Resolving irreconcilable spec vs normative conflicts (create gap instead).

See governance playbook in `platform/deployment/` when available.
